  "description": "XONRUP crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C80 H52 N10 O49 Tb8 4-,4(C8 H20 N1 1+),2(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Tb1 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb2 (Tb) has 9 O neighbors; Tb3 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb4 (Tb) has 9 O neighbors; Tb5 (Tb) has 9 O neighbors; Tb6 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb7 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb8 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 14 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.475-4.169 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 90.56-134.68°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula (Et4N)4[Tb8O(nd)8(NO3)10(H2O)2]·2MeCN. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 10 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
